# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase connection for LEDGER.
#
# Set BOTH to use Supabase Auth sign-in and the shared database
# (run supabase/schema.sql first — see DEPLOY.md).
# Leave BOTH blank to run in demo mode: a synthetic book stored in this
# browser, demo login demo@ecoloans.co.za / ledger-demo.
#
# Find these in your Supabase project: Settings → API
#   • Project URL             → VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#   • Project API key (anon)  → VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#
# The anon key is safe in a browser bundle: Row Level Security only lets
# signed-in, active team members read or write. Never put the service_role
# key here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
